And not all those years
were happy.

13:01.139 --> 13:03.340
Oh, sure, there were
some great times.

13:04.158 --> 13:05.392
Also, I want to build...

13:05.394 --> 13:08.261
But there were also
some bad times.

13:08.263 --> 13:09.563
Also some bad times.

13:09.565 --> 13:11.681
I mean, the point is,

13:11.683 --> 13:14.985
is that our relationship now
is just strictly business.

13:14.987 --> 13:17.587
Oh, speaking of which, we need
to upgrade the ventilation

13:17.589 --> 13:18.772
for the server farm.

13:18.774 --> 13:20.107
Oh, that's a good idea.

13:20.109 --> 13:21.992
Oh, also, I want to build
triple redundancy.

13:21.994 --> 13:24.277
Of course, but we shouldn't be
talking shop

13:24.279 --> 13:26.947
and leaving poor Zoey
out of the conversation.

13:26.949 --> 13:29.449
No, that's all right. I love
to hear about Walden's work.

13:29.451 --> 13:31.618
Oh, that's so sweet.

13:31.620 --> 13:34.704
I'm so glad
he found someone like you.

13:34.706 --> 13:37.090
Oh. Thank you.

13:37.092 --> 13:39.760
After I threw him out,
I wondered how he'd survive.

13:39.762 --> 13:40.994
He's so needy.

13:40.996 --> 13:42.379
I'm not needy.

13:42.381 --> 13:44.798
Yeah, you are.
BOTH: Yes, you are.

13:46.167 --> 13:47.300
So what's the deal?

13:47.302 --> 13:49.169
Are you guys in it
for the long haul,

13:49.171 --> 13:51.304
or are you just gonna date
and see what happens?

13:51.306 --> 13:54.357
Well, we're just finding
our way for the moment.

13:54.359 --> 13:55.859
(clears throat)
Oh, good.

13:55.861 --> 13:57.527
Mm.
Good.

13:57.529 --> 13:59.012
Keep it casual.

13:59.014 --> 14:01.314
That way no one can accuse you
of going after his money.

14:03.234 --> 14:04.584
Excuse me?

14:05.186 --> 14:07.287
I'm not after his money.

14:07.289 --> 14:09.489
Oh, no, you misunderstand.

14:09.491 --> 14:12.159
I... I'm sure you're not,
but unfortunately,

14:12.161 --> 14:13.910
there's no way to prove it.

14:15.213 --> 14:17.164
Luckily, I met him
when he had nothing,

14:17.166 --> 14:20.400
so there's no question
about my intentions.

14:20.402 --> 14:22.502
Are you questioning
my intentions?

14:22.504 --> 14:23.637
No, she's not. She's not.

14:23.639 --> 14:24.971
No, you're not.
You're not, are you?

14:24.973 --> 14:27.224
Of course not.

14:27.226 --> 14:29.009
Are &lt;i>you&lt;/i> questioning
my intentions?

14:29.011 --> 14:31.711
Me? No!

14:35.149 --> 14:37.184
Berta, how is
the pot roast coming?

14:37.186 --> 14:39.069
Got another 30 minutes.

14:39.071 --> 14:40.887
You guys keep chatting.

14:42.990 --> 14:44.858
♪ Men. ♪

14:44.860 --> 14:46.359
I don't understand.

14:46.361 --> 14:49.062
Why is my grandmother
living with his grandmother?

14:49.064 --> 14:51.081
Yeah, I was kind of
wondering that myself,

14:51.083 --> 14:52.999
but I didn't want
to look stupid.

14:53.001 --> 14:54.951
Too late, dude.

14:54.953 --> 14:56.536
You want to handle this, Alan?

14:56.538 --> 14:57.537
Not really.

14:57.539 --> 14:59.256
I wasn't asking.

14:59.258 --> 15:01.074
All right. Um...

15:01.076 --> 15:04.127
Well, fellas, um,

15:04.129 --> 15:08.265
your two grandmas are,
uh... are both very lonely,

15:08.267 --> 15:13.136
and so, they've, uh, decided
to become...

15:13.138 --> 15:15.138
uh, roommates, uh,

15:15.140 --> 15:17.357
and keep each other company.

15:17.359 --> 15:18.558
Oh, that makes sense.
Mm.

15:18.560 --> 15:20.110
Plus, if one of them
falls down,

15:20.112 --> 15:21.528
the other can call
the ambulance.

15:21.530 --> 15:24.314
What if they both fall down
at the same time?

15:24.316 --> 15:26.733
Um, I guess they starve
to death and die.

15:26.735 --> 15:29.402
Unless they go cannibal
and try to eat each other.

15:29.404 --> 15:30.620
If that happens,
I'm betting

15:30.622 --> 15:32.939
on my grandma
eating your grandma.

15:32.941 --> 15:34.774
Dude, there's no way
in the world

15:34.776 --> 15:36.776
that your grandma
eats my grandma.

15:36.778 --> 15:39.246
My grandma totally
eats your grandma.

15:39.248 --> 15:42.582
Nuh-uh. If any grandma's doing
any eating, it's my grandma.

15:42.584 --> 15:44.167
ELDRIDGE: No way.
JAKE: Come on.

15:44.169 --> 15:46.136
My grandma has real teeth.
You happy?

15:46.138 --> 15:47.304
ELDRIDGE:
How do you know?

15:47.306 --> 15:49.222
JAKE:
She bit me once.

15:50.641 --> 15:52.175
Well, that was great.

15:52.177 --> 15:55.111
I'm really glad we got
to spend some time together.

15:55.113 --> 15:56.897
Yeah, it was lovely.

15:56.899 --> 15:58.481
Yeah. Oh, don't forget

15:58.483 --> 16:00.734
we have that meeting
with the venture fund tomorrow.

16:00.736 --> 16:01.902
Oh, yeah, right.

16:01.904 --> 16:03.970
Bye.
Oh, bye.

16:03.972 --> 16:05.772
Oh, do me a favor, Zoey.

16:05.774 --> 16:08.191
Don't let him wear sandals
to the meeting.

16:08.193 --> 16:10.026
I really don't tell him
what to wear.

16:10.028 --> 16:12.229
That's okay. You'll learn.

16:13.864 --> 16:15.532
Don't wear sandals
to the meeting.

16:15.534 --> 16:17.083
Good night.
Good night.

16:17.085 --> 16:18.418
Night-night.
Bye. Drive safe.

16:18.420 --> 16:20.870
Mm.

16:20.872 --> 16:22.622
(sighs)
I think that went great.

16:22.624 --> 16:23.957
Do you?

16:23.959 --> 16:25.458
You don't?

16:25.460 --> 16:26.710
I don't.

16:26.712 --> 16:28.962
I don't, either.

16:30.348 --> 16:32.849
Did... Um, did I miss something?

16:32.851 --> 16:35.185
Obviously,
you missed everything.

16:35.187 --> 16:36.770
That horrible woman
won't be happy

16:36.772 --> 16:38.471
till she's destroyed
our relationship,

16:38.473 --> 16:39.806
and she has you back.

16:39.808 --> 16:41.274
What? No!

16:41.276 --> 16:43.009
She has a boyfriend.
She's happy.

16:43.011 --> 16:45.845
Oh, how can you be so smart
about some things

16:45.847 --> 16:48.181
and so &lt;i>stupid&lt;/i> about others?

16:48.183 --> 16:50.233
Okay, wait, just to be clear,

16:50.235 --> 16:53.519
what am I smart about
and what am I stupid about?!

16:55.172 --> 16:57.574
Oh, what?
Now you can't hear me!

16:57.576 --> 16:59.626
♪ Men. ♪

16:59.628 --> 17:02.162
Anybody want more
mashed potatoes?

17:02.164 --> 17:03.964
Oh, gosh, I'm
full, Jean,

17:03.966 --> 17:05.415
but everything's
so delicious.

17:05.417 --> 17:07.000
Thank you.

17:07.002 --> 17:09.836
And how lucky were you to
grow up with Mom's home cooking?

17:09.838 --> 17:12.305
Excuse me. You grew up
with home cooking, too.

17:12.307 --> 17:15.041
Yes, but the maid
did the cooking.

17:15.043 --> 17:17.344
It was still at home.

17:18.712 --> 17:21.214
Make sure
you leave room for dessert.

17:21.216 --> 17:22.649
I made pie.

17:22.651 --> 17:24.217
Oh, I love Grandma's pie.

17:25.653 --> 17:28.021
Yeah, yeah, I heard it, too.

17:28.023 --> 17:29.689
(clinking spoon on glass)

17:29.691 --> 17:32.325
There's something
I'd like to say.

17:32.327 --> 17:34.194
Oh, dear God, here it comes.

17:35.446 --> 17:40.033
It gives me such pleasure
to welcome Jean into my home

17:40.035 --> 17:43.787
and to share our new friendship
with our two families.

17:43.789 --> 17:46.039
Hear, hear.
Hear, hear.

17:46.041 --> 17:47.424
Hear, hear.

17:47.426 --> 17:50.543
And I'd just like to thank Evy
for showing me

17:50.545 --> 17:54.164
that it's never too late to
teach an old dog new tricks.

17:56.050 --> 17:58.751
Certainly didn't teach
her to fetch a bone.

17:58.753 --> 18:00.186
Shh.

18:01.588 --> 18:03.273
I have a question.

18:03.275 --> 18:05.175
Oh, God, here it comes.

18:06.193 --> 18:08.194
If you and her
were cannibals,

18:08.196 --> 18:10.980
which do you think
would eat the other?

18:13.984 --> 18:17.687
There you have it:
the upside of stupid.

18:22.109 --> 18:24.544
ZOEY: I'm sorry, Walden,
but Bridget's right.

18:24.546 --> 18:26.713
You have history with her;
you have none with me.

18:26.715 --> 18:28.715
You can't even be sure
I love you for yourself

18:28.717 --> 18:29.782
and not your money.

18:29.784 --> 18:30.967
What are you saying?

18:30.969 --> 18:32.802
I'm saying,
I think it might be better

18:32.804 --> 18:35.171
for both of us
if we went our separate ways.

18:35.173 --> 18:37.307
Okay, that's one approach...

18:37.309 --> 18:39.809
which stinks.

18:39.811 --> 18:43.313
So, let me make
a counterproposal.

18:43.315 --> 18:45.631
Why don't you move in with me?

18:45.633 --> 18:48.184
What?

18:48.186 --> 18:50.019
Yeah, you and Ava
move in with me.

18:50.021 --> 18:52.439
I love you,
and I want you in my life,

18:52.441 --> 18:54.858
I want... I want
to have a future with you.

18:54.860 --> 18:57.143
Really?

18:57.145 --> 18:58.495
Really.

18:58.497 --> 19:00.947
AVA: Mummy, Mummy,
please say yes!

19:00.949 --> 19:04.117
What are you doing
out of bed?!

19:04.119 --> 19:07.120
I love you, Walden!

19:07.122 --> 19:09.155
I love you, Ava.

19:09.157 --> 19:11.824
Get back into bed!

19:11.826 --> 19:13.126
Hmm. Let's see.

19:13.128 --> 19:16.513
So, that's one vote for yes,
and I vote yes,

19:16.515 --> 19:19.215
so, the motion is passed.

19:19.217 --> 19:22.602
There is one
tiny little problem.

19:22.604 --> 19:23.603
What's that?

19:23.605 --> 19:25.972
If Ava and I move in,

19:25.974 --> 19:29.843
isn't somebody going
to have to move out?

19:30.661 --> 19:33.446
Hmm.

19:34.698 --> 19:36.232
(groans)

19:36.234 --> 19:38.351
What's the matter?
I don't know.

19:38.353 --> 19:41.538
Just felt a little shiver
go down my spine.

19:41.540 --> 19:43.706
(groans)

19:52.181 --> 19:53.765
♪ Men. ♪

19:53.767 --> 19:55.817
Here you go.

19:55.819 --> 19:57.652
I got to ask.

19:57.654 --> 19:59.521
What's with the tea?

19:59.523 --> 20:01.473
You make it for me.
You make it for Lyndsey.

20:01.475 --> 20:02.941
Well, I've got
a little philosophy.

20:02.943 --> 20:04.076
When someone's nice enough

20:04.078 --> 20:06.278
to let me into their home
or their pants,

20:06.280 --> 20:07.612
I like to show my appreciation.

20:07.614 --> 20:09.281
Without spending
any money.

20:09.283 --> 20:11.816
You know me so well.

20:11.818 --> 20:13.452
So, recap.

20:13.454 --> 20:14.703
How'd your dinner go?

20:14.705 --> 20:15.954
Oh, pretty well, actually.

20:15.956 --> 20:17.756
The grandmas were
on their best behavior,

20:17.758 --> 20:19.875
and the two boys--
well, let's just say,

20:19.877 --> 20:23.512
they're gonna be living with us
for a long, long time. And you?

20:23.514 --> 20:25.597
Oh, good, good.
It went really good.

20:25.599 --> 20:28.016
So, everything's okay with Zoey?
Yeah, it's fantastic.

20:28.018 --> 20:30.685
Sounds like everything's great
with you and Lyndsey, huh?

20:30.687 --> 20:32.304
Oh, yeah, more than good.

20:32.306 --> 20:34.473
Oh, forgot the honey.

20:36.476 --> 20:38.443
She owns her own home, right?

20:38.445 --> 20:39.778
Yeah.

20:39.780 --> 20:41.696
(groans)

20:41.698 --> 20:44.983
Hmm. Think I may be coming down
with something.

20:44.985 --> 20:48.985
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

00:00.500 --> 00:02.000
